  "finalText": "All 33 task-related tests pass. The 2 pre-existing failures (`date.test.ts`, `advanced.test.ts`, `modules.test.ts`) are unrelated.\n\n## Summary\n\n**Root cause**: The `GET /api/tasks` endpoint relied solely on the repository's SQL `WHERE user_id = $1` filter for ownership. There was no defensive guard in the service layer, and zero tests verifying that a user only sees their own tasks. If the repository method were ever swapped (e.g., to `findByAssignedTo` which filters only by `assigned_to` with no `user_id` guard), tasks would leak across users silently.\n\n**Fix** (`src/services/taskService.ts:67`): Added a defensive `tasks.filter(task => task.userId === userId)` after the repository call in `TaskService.findAll`. This ensures only the authenticated user's tasks are returned regardless of what the repository returns.\n\n**Regression tests** (6 new tests):\n\n| File | Test | What it verifies |\n|---|---|---|\n| `tests/task.test.ts` | `should not return tasks belonging to other users` | Service filters out other users' tasks even if the repository returns them |\n| `tests/taskRoutes.test.ts` | `should return only the authenticated user tasks (happy path)` | Happy path: user sees their tasks |\n| `tests/taskRoutes.test.ts` | `should not return tasks belonging to other users` | Route-level: user A cannot see user B's tasks |\n| `tests/taskRoutes.test.ts` | `should call findByUser with the authenticated user id` | Correct userId is passed through the stack |",
